    {
      "gap": "Systematic failure mode taxonomy — WHY does recursive decomposition bottom out, and what makes a problem fundamentally hard for current systems?",
      "evidence": "Hilbert fails on 2 miniF2F problems and 30% of PutnamBench but provides no systematic taxonomy of failure types. AlphaProof's combinatorics weakness is noted but unexplained. Understanding whether failures are due to bad decompositions, correct but unprovable subgoals, Lean type system limitations, or missing Mathlib theorems would directly inform next-generation systems.",
