      "what_it_does": "Feeds specific Lean compiler error messages (not just pass/fail) back into the model's context for self-correction, enabling targeted repair of near-correct proofs. Ablations show the specific error content is crucial — binary failure signal alone is much less effective.",
      "used_by": ["Goedel-Prover-V2", "Aristotle", "Hilbert"],
      "could_be_applied_to": "Any generation task with structured error feedback — code generation with compiler/linter errors, SQL generation with database error messages, API integration with response error codes"
